# Runtime state and build artifacts. Never commit these.
#
# One pattern per line, and NO trailing comments on a pattern line. gitignore does not support
# them: an earlier version of this file had comments after the patterns, which made the comment
# part of the pattern, so nothing here matched anything. Verify with:
#     git check-ignore -v state logs voices .venv
state/
logs/
audio/
voices/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Local edits and backups people leave behind
*.orig
*.orig.bak
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.bak-wakeword-*
*.pre-*
.worktrees/
# private operating notes: these live in ~/.hermes/skills, not in a published repo
skills/

# Private and upstream material: these are kept inside the backup mirror, deliberately outside this
# tree, and the mirror's pruning protects them there. Nothing here should ever be committed: the
# enclosure files are a third-party design whose licence forbids redistribution, and the device image
# and token copy are ours alone.
/private/
/upstream/
